From c0e30b0233b111afcc31c6c4980d5f40b181c34f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 05:03:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] klzh2: khuf blocks for long code chunks at levels 1-4
 (mode 3 from 1024 symbols), chunks of at most 128 Ki symbols

Decode time of the code streams was the tANS symbol loop (one symbol per table lookup);
khuf's decoder takes two per lookup on blocks of 4096 symbols or more. Mode 3 of a code
chunk now means the predefined tANS table under 1024 symbols (as before: no earlier frame
has a longer mode-3 chunk) and a khuf block from 1024 on. The encoder writes one at levels
1-4 for chunks of 16384 symbols or more when khuf's real size is within 1/64 of the tANS
estimate. Six Silesia files, level 3 (dec_time, indicative): 47,622,616 -> 47,680,142 bytes
(+0.12%), stream decode 61.8 -> 54.2 ms, whole decode 176.3 -> 170.5 ms. Levels 5-9 keep
tANS only. A frozen frame with this chunk kind (tests/klzh2_frames2.h); the first set is
untouched and still decodes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUEN4aRWhUw7yL7cZMqTmZ
